Summary: ncacn_ip_udp endpoint family declaration invalid

Many thanks for all the excellent assistance in resolving my 
DCE rpc problem. I've received responses which I will summarize from:

  gjb@fig.citib.com (Greg Brail)
  Phil_Hirsch@transarc.com
  "Helmut Duschinger (CIP 90)" <htduschi@cip.informatik.uni-erlangen.de>
  Johannes Kroupa <kroupa@argos.kapsch.co.at>
  Kevin Coffman <kwc@citi.umich.edu>

Concerning what does "Exception: status 0x16c9a042 (dce / rpc)" mean:

(1) The error code 0x16c9a042 is to be found in it's decimal equivalent
    in the /usr/include/dce/rpcsts.h file and translates to:
      rpc_s_connect_rejected.  

DEC if you are listening, the online manuals explanation for that 
error code could be more enlightening and the IDL manual merely says an
error will result at runtime if the endpoint family declaration isn't valid.


(2) Set the NLSPATH environment variable to /usr/lib/nls/msg/en_US.88591/%N
    in order to have the error code messages translated to the 
    English text messages.  

This is documented in the online manual for dce_error_inq_text().
I've tried setting the NLSPATH environment variable and had no luck
in getting the dce_error_inq_text() function to spit out the
proper text.  The file /usr/lib/nls/msg/en_US.88591/dcerpc.cat 
contains the error message text, so that is still a puzzle.


(3) The endpoint family "ncacn_ip_udp" is invalid. Valid families
    are "ncacn_ip_tcp" and "ncadp_ip_udp".  This is 
    documented in 17.7.3 of the DCE application development Guide.

Using the correct endpoint family "ncadg_ip_udp" fixed the 
programs and the rpc client and server are now working.

