The problem I had with getting text messages from dce_error_inq_text()
was that both the NLSPATH and LANG enviroment variables must be defined.

The relevant excerpt from the DEC man page for dce_error_inq_text() reads:

  Before calling this routine, the environment variable NLSPATH must be set
  to point to DCE message catalog files.  A general C-shell command to set
  this environment variable follows:

       % setenv NLSPATH dceshared/nls/msg/LANG/%N

  Note that LANG is a variable instead of a literal.  A specific example of
  this general command follows:

       % setenv NLSPATH /usr/lib/nls/msg/en_US.88591/%N

This should be ammended to include setting the LANG variable as well.

       % setenv LANG en_SU.88591

Thanks to Henry Lee of IBM DCE development for his assistance in
pinpointing the the LANG variable requirement. 


