Phew. I think I got the original version of the alpha switching code
from David Keppel, but the version I got from him has a series of
loads followed by a series of stores.  In general, I interleave the
loads and stores because back-to-back loads always seem to cause
problems on RISC machines. Since a context switch routine doesn't do
much other than loads and stores, interleaving the loads means you
need to interleave the stores as well -- and I ordered them to take
advantage of the write-buffers on the alpha.


