The End User Forum is hosted by the End User Steering Committee. The
objectives of the Steering Committee are to express and publicize end user
requirements and to facilitate the development of OSF technologies which
meet these requirements. Over the past several years, the Steering
Committee has interacted with the senior staff of OSF and with other OSF
membership constituencies in order to accelerate successful delivery of
open systems in a way that represents consumer interests, conveys
appropriate urgency, and communicates an end user vision of open systems.

To the End User member, the End User Forum represents an additional way to
make one's voice heard by OSF and the industry at large. The EU Forum and
Steering Committee can focus OSF priorities on areas where interests of
large numbers of end user members coincide, ensuring that these areas get
the attention end users require. The Steering Committee had an active year
in 1993 and has plans for even greater visibility and impact for 1994. Your
participation and input are critical to this effort.

Pre-registration for this free event is requested so that we may plan for
your participation. Please contact Marcie Becker, Communications Manager OSF 
Membership Programs. Marcie will coordinate member participation in this event. 
Please contact her at 617-621-8793 or becker@osf.org if you have any questions.

