As trevor correctly observed the LDQ $31, address is thrown away

From page 3-1 of the Alpha Architecture reference manual

For all cases except Unconditional branch and Jump instructions, results of
an instruction that specifies R31 as the destination operand are
discarded. Also it is UNPREDICTABLE whether the other destination
operands (implicit and explicit) are changed by the instruction. It is
implementation dependent to what extent the instruction is actually executed
once it has been fetched. It is also UNPREDICTABLE whether exceptions are
signalled during the execution of such an instruction.

I believe the DECChip 20164 discards the R31 target LDQ at the issue
stage. This would explain the anamolies you have been seeing. Try loading
your data into some register other than R31 to see more consistent behavior.

/murari


