On post 1.0.2 versions of DCE, you can pretty much consider the Master
CDS server to be 'the cds server that has the master replica of the
root directory'. In order to move the master CDS server, you need only
replicate all of the directories to a secondary CDS server, and change the
master for the directories to the slave. At this point, the machine
that had been the slave is now the 'Master'. You should be able to
do a 'cdscp delete clearinghouse /.:/XXX_ch', and then deconfig
the machine.

Note: Not all vendors fully support the above -- your mileage may vary. Be
sure
that both servers are at least at 1.0.2 before trying this.

