In article <2m7sgp$23u@news.u.washington.edu>,
Steven Noyd Jones <noyd@u.washington.edu> wrote:

>When I run the client, the "rpc_call_start()" routine in the client 
>stub returns with the error status 0x16c9a042, and triggers a core 
>dump.  When I run the server, the "rpc_server_listen()" routine in my 
>server "main()" program returns with the error status 0x16c9a042 and 
>continues.  

The error code you mentioned is "connection request rejected". 

>[ 
>uuid(5DBA73AC-264D-0000-028C-8E3802000000),
>version(1),
>endpoint("ncacn_ip_udp:[617]")
>] 

"ncacn_ip_udp" isn't a valid protocol sequence. All DCE
implementations that I know of support "ncadg_ip_udp", and some also
support "ncacn_ip_tcp". Your use of this as your protocol is certainly
part of the problem.

>  strcpy(line,"ncacn_ip_tcp:goren1.u.washington.edu[endpoint=617]");

Is that a legal string binding? Try taking out the "endpoint=" and see
if that helps. But this will never work unless you change the protocol
of the endpoint in your .idl file to a valid protocol sequence, like I
mentioned above. Good luck!

				greg

